{
  "title": "79: al-Naazea'at النازعات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالنّٰزِعٰتِ غَرْقًا ۙ‏(1)\n\nBy those who drag forth violently\nوَّالنّٰشِطٰتِ نَشْطًا ۙ‏(2)\n\nAnd those who untie (the knot) briskly\nوَّالسّٰبِحٰتِ سَبْحًا ۙ‏(3)\n\nAnd those who glide on (Swiftly)\nفَالسّٰبِقٰتِ سَبْقًا ۙ‏(4)\n\nThen those who go ahead with a foremost speed\nفَالْمُدَبِّرٰتِ اَمْرًا‌ ۘ‏(5)\n\nThen those who (submissively) manage the affairs\nيَوْمَ تَرْجُفُ الرَّاجِفَةُ ۙ‏(6)\n\nOn the day on which shall quake the quaking\nتَتْبَعُهَا الرَّادِفَةُ ؕ‏(7)\n\nShall follow it the quake (by the second trumpet) which shall follow\nقُلُوْبٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ وَّاجِفَةٌ ۙ‏(8)\n\nHearts that day shall palpitate\nاَبْصَارُهَا خَاشِعَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(9)\n\nTheir eyes shall be cast down\nيَقُوْلُوْنَ ءَاِنَّا لَمَرْدُوْدُوْنَ فِى الْحَافِرَةِ ؕ‏(10)\n\nThey shall say (then): ‘‘What! Shall we indeed be restored to as (we were) at first?\nءَاِذَا كُنَّا عِظَامًا نَّخِرَةً ؕ‏(11)\n\nWhat! When we are (even) bones rotten?\nقَالُوْا تِلْكَ اِذًا كَرَّةٌ خَاسِرَةٌ‌ ۘ‏(12)\n\nThey said: ‘‘That then will be a return in vain\nفَاِنَّمَا هِىَ زَجْرَةٌ وَّاحِدَةٌ ۙ‏(13)\n\nVerily, it shall be but a single (violent) blast\nفَاِذَا هُمْ بِالسَّاهِرَةِ ؕ‏(14)\n\nWhen lo! they shall (all) be in the awakened state\nهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ مُوْسٰى‌ۘ‏(15)\n\nHath not come unto thee the story of Moses?\nاِذْ نَادٰٮهُ رَبُّهٗ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًى‌ۚ‏(16)\n\nWhen called him his Lord in the Holy Valley (called) ‘Tuva\nاِذْهَبْ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى ۖ‏(17)\n\n(Saying)-. ‘‘Go thou (O’ Moses!) unto Pharaoh! verily, he hath transgressed the bounds!\nفَقُلْ هَلْ لَّكَ اِلٰٓى اَنْ تَزَكّٰى ۙ‏(18)\n\nAnd say (unto him)’. ‘‘Hast thou (a desire) to cleanse thyself (of thy disbelief)?\nوَاَهْدِيَكَ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ فَتَخْشٰى‌ۚ‏(19)\n\nAnd I will guide thee unto thy Lord so that thou mayest fear him\nفَاَرٰٮهُ الْاٰيَةَ الْكُبْرٰى ۖ‏(20)\n\nAnd he showed him the greatest sign (miracle)\nفَكَذَّبَ وَعَصٰى ۖ‏(21)\n\nBut belied he and disobeyed\nثُمَّ اَدْبَرَ يَسْعٰىۖ‏(22)\n\nThen turned he his back hastily\nفَحَشَرَ فَنَادٰىۖ‏(23)\n\nAnd gathered (the people) and proclaimed\nفَقَالَ اَنَا رَبُّكُمُ الْاَعْلٰى ۖ‏(24)\n\nAnd said ‘‘I am your Lord, the most High!\nفَاَخَذَهُ اللّٰهُ نَكَالَ الْاٰخِرَةِ وَالْاُوْلٰى ؕ‏(25)\n\nSo seized him God, with the chastisement in the hereafter, and the life before (it)\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِّمَنْ يَّخْشٰىؕ‏(26)\n\nVerily in this there is a lesson unto him who feareth (God).\nءَاَنْتُمْ اَشَدُّ خَلْقًا اَمِ السَّمَآءُ‌ ؕ بَنٰٮهَا‏(27)\n\nAre ye the harder to be created, or the heaven which built He?\nرَفَعَ سَمْكَهَا فَسَوَّٮهَا ۙ‏(28)\n\nRaised He its heights and established it\nوَ اَغْطَشَ لَيْلَهَا وَاَخْرَجَ ضُحٰٮهَا‏(29)\n\nAnd He darkened its night, and brought forth its noon light\nوَالْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ دَحٰٮهَا ؕ‏(30)\n\nAnd the earth, afterwards he stretched forth\nاَخْرَجَ مِنْهَا مَآءَهَا وَمَرْعٰٮهَا‏(31)\n\nHe brought forth from it, its waters and its pasteurage\nوَالْجِبَالَ اَرْسٰٮهَا ۙ‏(32)\n\nAnd the mountains, He set them firm\nمَتَاعًا لَّكُمْ وَلِاَنْعَامِكُمْؕ‏(33)\n\nA provision for you and your cattle\nفَاِذَا جَآءَتِ الطَّآمَّةُ الْكُبْرٰى ۖ‏(34)\n\nWhen cometh the Great Calamity.\nيَوْمَ يَتَذَكَّرُ الْاِنْسَانُ مَا سَعٰىۙ‏(35)\n\nThe day when man shall recollect (all) that he strove for\nوَبُرِّزَتِ الْجَحِيْمُ لِمَنْ يَّرٰى‏(36)\n\nAnd the hell shall be displayed unto him who seeth\nفَاَمَّا مَنْ طَغٰىۙ‏(37)\n\nThen, as for him who hath transgressed the bounds\nوَاٰثَرَ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ۙ‏(38)\n\nAnd preferreth the life of this world\nفَاِنَّ الْجَحِيْمَ هِىَ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(39)\n\nThen, verily, Hell, that shall be his abode\nوَاَمَّا مَنْ خَافَ مَقَامَ رَبِّهٖ وَ نَهَى النَّفْسَ عَنِ الْهَوٰىۙ‏(40)\n\nAnd as for him who feareth the standing of his Lord, and forbiddeth (his) self from (following) his inclinations\nفَاِنَّ الْجَنَّةَ هِىَ الْمَاْوٰىؕ‏(41)\n\nThen, verily, the Garden (of Paradise), that shall be his abode\nيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ السَّاعَةِ اَيَّانَ مُرْسٰٮهَا ؕ‏(42)\n\nThey ask thee of ‘the Hour’ whereto (is) anchorage?\nفِيْمَ اَنْتَ مِنْ ذِكْرٰٮهَاؕ‏(43)\n\nWherein art thou of its notion?\nاِلٰى رَبِّكَ مُنْتَهٰٮهَاؕ‏(44)\n\nUnto thy Lord (alone) is its termination!\nاِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ مُنْذِرُ مَنْ يَّخْشٰٮهَاؕ‏(45)\n\nThou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) art only a Warner unto him who feareth it\nكَاَنَّهُمْ يَوْمَ يَرَوْنَهَا لَمْ يَلْبَثُوْۤا اِلَّا عَشِيَّةً اَوْ ضُحٰٮهَا‏(46)\n\nIt shall seem unto them, on the day when they see it, as though they tarried not in (their graves) but a (single) evening, or the following morning",
  "merits": "Surah al-Naazea’at (Those Who Pull Out)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 42 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward for reciting this Surah is ten times the number of entities in the Heavens."
